macOS 27 support — Ice/MenuBar/MacOS27, Shared/Services changes made for it,
Package.swift, and Tests/IceMacOS27CoreTests — comes from Ice pull request #995,
"Restore hiding, the Ice Bar and the layout editor on macOS 27", by
RabenkoYevhenii (https://github.com/jordanbaird/Ice/pull/995),
Copyright (C) 2026 RabenkoYevhenii, licensed under GPL-3.0.

Changes made in this fork (GPL-3.0 §5(a)), all dated 2026-11-11:

- Merged Ice PR #995 onto upstream main (commit 11edd391) and committed it as
  762165f5.
- Renamed the product to BarMan (PRODUCT_NAME in Ice.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj)
  and the shared scheme to BarMan.xcscheme.
- Changed the bundle identifiers from com.jordanbaird.Ice and
  com.jordanbaird.Ice.MenuBarItemService to com.macutils.barman and
  com.macutils.barman.MenuBarItemService, and updated
  Shared/Services/MenuBarItemService.swift to match.
- Reset MARKETING_VERSION to 1.0.0 and CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION to 1.
- Replaced user-facing "Ice" branding with "BarMan" in the settings panes, the
  permissions window, the right-click menu, the window titles, and the Ice Bar
  (now "BarMan Bar"). Functional identifiers were left unchanged:
  Ice.ControlItem.*, the asset names, the persisted control-item image names,
  and the "Ice/ItemImages" cache directory.
- Replaced the About pane's upstream donate, contribute, and report-a-bug links
  with an attribution link to Ice, and added an in-app "Based on Ice" credit.
- Replaced NSHumanReadableCopyright with a notice naming both the BarMan
  copyright holder and the original Ice copyright holder.
- Removed the upstream Sparkle appcast URL from Ice/Resources/Info.plist; the
  updater now starts only when SUFeedURL is present, so BarMan never offers
  upstream Ice builds as updates.

